  "notes": "One of three common verbs pronounced おかす, each written with a different kanji and carrying a distinct meaning. {侵|おか}す specifically means to intrude upon, invade, or violate (territory, rights, or bodily integrity).\n\nTHE THREE おかす VERBS:\n- {侵|おか}す — to invade, to violate (territory, rights)\n- {犯|おか}す — to commit (a crime), to offend against\n- {冒|おか}す — to risk, to brave (danger); to desecrate\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {領土|りょうど}を{侵|おか}す — to invade territory\n- {人権|じんけん}を{侵|おか}す — to violate human rights\n- {主権|しゅけん}を{侵|おか}す — to infringe on sovereignty\n- プライバシーを{侵|おか}す — to violate privacy\n- {体|からだ}を{侵|おか}す — to attack the body (of disease)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {侵害|しんがい} — infringement, violation (noun form)\n- {侵入|しんにゅう} — intrusion, trespassing\n- {侵略|しんりゃく} — invasion, aggression",
